{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall write Aaron's name on the staff of Levi, etc.</b> From the fact that He did not previously command taking a staff for the tribe of Levi, it indicates that it is included within the twelve staffs that He spoke of nearby — twelve staffs, and the staff of Levi is included within the twelve. And it is possible to say that this is what they did: they took one piece of wood and divided it into twelve parts, and each tribe took its portion from the same wood, and there was no difference between Aaron's and any of the others — for only in this way would the test be valid. And through this the verse's statement is made precise: <b>And all their princes gave them to him, etc.</b> <b>And Aaron's staff was among their staffs</b> — meaning, one portion from the same piece of wood from which they took their staffs. Afterwards, the statement of our Rabbies of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 18:23) came to my hand, and they said as we have said."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:45.009375331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}